---
import { site } from '../../site.config';
const faqs = [
	{ q: 'Is Sirius free?', a: 'Yes. Sirius is free to download and use on any number of devices you own, for personal or commercial development. There are no plans and no tiers: you bring your own model keys and pay the provider directly, or run local models and pay nothing.' },
	{ q: 'Which models can I use?', a: 'Anthropic Claude, Google Gemini, OpenAI, OpenRouter, Groq, DeepSeek, Mistral and xAI through their APIs; Ollama, LM Studio, llama.cpp and vLLM locally; and any other OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Pick a model with Ctrl+Shift+M or from the picker in the chat.' },
	{ q: 'Does my code leave my machine?', a: 'Only in the request you send, and only to the provider you chose: the prompt, the context you attached or the editor included, and files a tool read. Sirius runs no relay. With a local model, nothing leaves the machine at all. There is no telemetry, no crash reporting and no account.' },
	{ q: 'Is this Visual Studio Code?', a: 'No. Sirius is a derivative work of Code - OSS, the MIT-licensed open-source foundation of VS Code; it is not VS Code and is neither produced nor endorsed by Microsoft. It does not use Microsoft\'s branding, telemetry or Marketplace: extensions come from Open VSX, because Microsoft\'s marketplace terms bar other products from using theirs.' },
	{ q: 'Can I bring my extensions and settings?', a: 'Yes. Sirius: Import from VS Code, Cursor, or Windsurf brings your settings, keybindings, snippets and extensions over from Visual Studio Code, Cursor, Windsurf (now Devin Desktop) or VSCodium, and reports what it imported.' },
	{ q: 'Where are my API keys stored?', a: 'In your operating system\'s keyring — libsecret on Linux, the Keychain on macOS, the Credential Manager on Windows — through the editor\'s secret storage. Never in settings.json, never synchronised, never sent anywhere but the provider they belong to.' },
	{ q: 'How does it update?', a: 'The tarball and the Windows installer check the update server and update themselves (Windows in place; on Linux the editor notifies you and opens the download page). The .deb, .rpm and Arch packages update through your package manager; the pacman repository is updated by the release itself.' },
	{ q: 'Why does Windows warn me on first run?', a: 'The Windows installer is not code-signed yet, so SmartScreen shows its warning. Choose More info, then Run anyway. Every release asset is attested with GitHub build provenance and carries a sha256 sidecar you can verify. Signing is on the roadmap.' },
	{ q: 'Is there a macOS build?', a: 'Not yet. The packaging exists, but a macOS release needs an Apple Developer certificate for signing and notarisation; without it Gatekeeper refuses the app. Follow the GitHub issue to hear when it ships.' },
	{ q: 'Is Sirius open source?', a: 'No. Sirius ships under its own proprietary licence, and its source is published on GitHub. Code - OSS and every third-party component keep their own licences, reproduced in ThirdPartyNotices.txt.' },
];
---
<section class="section faq" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
	<div class="container grid">
		<div class="head">
			<p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
			<h2 id="faq-title">Questions, <span class="muted">answered plainly.</span></h2>
			<p class="lede">Anything missing? <a href={site.issues} rel="noopener">Ask on GitHub</a>.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="list">
			{faqs.map((f) => (
				<details class="item">
					<summary><span>{f.q}</span><span class="chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary>
					<p>{f.a}</p>
				</details>
			))}
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
	'@context': 'https://schema.org',
	'@type': 'FAQPage',
	mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
})} />

<style>
	.grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr); gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem); align-items: start; }
	.head h2 { margin-top: 1rem; }
	.head .lede { margin-top: 1rem; font-size: var(--text-m); }
	.list { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
	.item { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
	summary { list-style: none; cursor: pointer; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; padding: 1.1rem 0; font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--text-m); color: var(--fg); }
	summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
	summary:hover { color: var(--accent-text); }
	.chev { flex: none; width: 10px; height: 10px; border-right: 2px solid var(--fg-dim); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--fg-dim); transform: rotate(45deg); transition: transform 0.2s; margin-right: 4px; }
	.item[open] .chev { transform: rotate(-135deg); }
	.item p { padding: 0 0 1.25rem; color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.6; font-size: var(--text-s); max-width: 70ch; }
	@media (max-width: 900px) { .grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
</style>
